#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =============================================================================
# overall_forecast.py
# Standalone (no Streamlit / no UI) overall-only forecaster for GLC Sales
# Order data -- the company-wide total, not broken out by customer/material.
# =============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS IS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   The simplest of the three related scripts:
#     - production_forecasting_mvp.py  = full interactive Streamlit app
#     - batch_forecast_comparison.py   = batch job across 800+ customer/
#                                         material combinations, SQLite +
#                                         one Excel file for the overall total
#     - overall_forecast.py (this one) = JUST the overall total, no
#                                         customer/material breakdown, no
#                                         database -- one Excel file, in and
#                                         out in well under a minute.
#
#   Forecasts the next 21 days (default) of daily Net Pounds across the
#   whole business, using the same 4 models as the other two scripts
#   (Seasonal Naive, AutoARIMA, AutoETS, HistGradientBoostingRegressor --
#   Chronos-2 is not included here either), plus the average of those 4.
#   Known future backlog (already-booked orders with a future Mat.avail.dt)
#   is folded in as a floor, same logic as the other two scripts. Output is
#   one Excel workbook: the forecast table (comma-formatted, no decimals)
#   plus a backtest-accuracy sheet.
#
# INSTALLATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   pip install pandas numpy openpyxl scikit-learn statsforecast scipy
#
# RUN
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   python overall_forecast.py --workbook "Sales Order 2024-26.xlsx"
#
#   Flags (all optional, see --help):
#     --excel-out overall_forecast.xlsx   output file
#     --horizon 21                        forecast horizon in days
#     --n-windows 8                       preferred backtest windows
#     --thorough-arima                    full AutoARIMA search (slower,
#                                          modestly more accurate) instead
#                                          of the faster default
#     --as-of YYYY-MM-DD                  historical cutoff (default: today)
#
# =============================================================================

